# Cursor AI Rules

You are an autonomous AI coding assistant in this repository. Follow these strict rules:

## ⚡ Autonomous Auto-Pilot
When given a feature request or bug report:
1. Don't ask unnecessary questions; plan tests and structure upfront.
2. Write automated tests first in `tests/`.
3. Implement clean, modular code.
4. Run `./run.ps1 check` (or `./run.sh check`) and resolve all test failures and lint issues automatically.
5. Report completion with verified results.

## 1. Quality & Verification
- JDK 17 & Android SDK (API 35) are installed locally. To preserve GitHub Actions minutes, always run `./run.ps1 test` or `.\gradlew.bat :app:testDebugUnitTest` locally.
- Execute `./run.ps1 test` (or `.\gradlew.bat :app:testDebugUnitTest`) after modifying code.
- Verify tests pass before reporting completion.
- Verify APK build with `./run.ps1 build` (or `.\gradlew.bat assembleDebug`) when modifying app packaging.

## 2. Architecture & Standards
- Keep functions small, modular, and single-purpose.
- Strict type safety: use type annotations wherever supported.
- Preserve existing comments and docstrings.

## 3. Subagents & Multi-Agent Collaboration
- Proactively use subagents/background agents for deep codebase research, edge-case analysis, and independent adversarial code review to maximize accuracy and code quality.

## 4. UI/UX & Copywriting (Anti-AI-Slop)
- Do NOT use exaggerated emojis (🔥, 🚀, ✨, 🎉, etc.) or marketing buzzwords ("🔥急上昇しています", "爆速", "革新的").
- Keep UI text concise, functional, and factual (e.g. use "トレンド" instead of "🔥いま話題！").
- Eliminate decorative fluff and unnecessary filler text.
